WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:03.818
Probate is the court process of settling

2
00:00:03.818 --> 00:00:05.624
someone's estate.

3
00:00:05.624 --> 00:00:07.683
Timelines vary a lot,

4
00:00:07.683 --> 00:00:11.100
but here is the usual path.

5
00:00:11.350 --> 00:00:13.029
First, the will,

6
00:00:13.029 --> 00:00:14.608
if there is one,

7
00:00:14.608 --> 00:00:19.746
is filed, and the court appoints a personal representative.

8
00:00:19.746 --> 00:00:23.100
That often takes a few weeks.

9
00:00:23.350 --> 00:00:26.923
Next, creditors and heirs are notified.

10
00:00:26.923 --> 00:00:30.496
There is a set window for creditor claims,

11
00:00:30.496 --> 00:00:33.100
often several months.

12
00:00:33.350 --> 00:00:36.351
The representative inventories assets,

13
00:00:36.351 --> 00:00:38.164
may order appraisals,

14
00:00:38.164 --> 00:00:41.600
and pays valid debts and taxes.

15
00:00:41.850 --> 00:00:46.330
A final income tax return is needed for the person

16
00:00:46.330 --> 00:00:47.579
who died.

17
00:00:47.579 --> 00:00:51.031
Sometimes the estate itself has to file

18
00:00:51.031 --> 00:00:53.100
returns too.

19
00:00:53.350 --> 00:00:56.178
When the court is satisfied,

20
00:00:56.178 --> 00:01:00.401
assets go to the people named in the will,

21
00:01:00.401 --> 00:01:04.100
or to heirs under state law.

22
00:01:04.350 --> 00:01:07.119
Then the estate is closed.

23
00:01:07.119 --> 00:01:10.786
A simple one can take under a year.

24
00:01:10.786 --> 00:01:16.100
A contested or complex one can take much longer.

25
00:01:16.350 --> 00:01:19.519
If you are handling an estate,

26
00:01:19.519 --> 00:01:22.167
our checklist can help.

27
00:01:22.167 --> 00:01:27.100
We are glad to talk when you are ready.
